WEBVTT

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:09.020
These are the glasses you'd wear for show?

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:12.760
A Few Years Prior

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:14.290
Mr. Rizzo introduced you to quite the restaurant.

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:16.670
But it looks like a nice place.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:19.500
And I really like Claudio, the man who gave these glasses to me.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.960
He's a real gentleman.

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:24.510
Claudio?

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:28.980
Furio,

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:33.330
I'd like to introduce you to someone sent here on the owner and the Madam's recommendation.

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:34.760
Sure thing.

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:38.740
I suppose I should put these on, huh?

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:44.040
Yes, I think she'll like that.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:46.310
Very well, then.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:52.440
So? Have you gotten used to the restaurant yet?

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.350
Yes, I certainly have.

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:58.480
This place has fewer staff than the other places I've worked, so I find it easier.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:02.420
What about the fact so many aspiring chefs come here wanting to train

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:04.240
because they've heard you're employed here?

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:05.950
Now, I don't know about all that.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.730
Just let me know if anything ever bothers you.

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:13.610
I'm always available to talk to, should you ever need to.

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:21.510
Speaking of these glasses... Why is he so nice to me?

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:25.910
It looks to me that Claudio knows you somehow.

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:30.510
That's the impression I got when the owner first mentioned your name.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.540
Seriously?

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:39.230
Those glasses look fantastic on you.

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:40.710
So handsome.

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:43.030
You're too kind, Madam.

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:44.610
This is Furio.

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:48.030
He started as our head chef last week.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:50.290
What made you choose dell'orso?

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:54.500
Well, it was on Mr. Rizzo's recommendation.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:02:00.700
<i>He's so soft-spoken... Old Man Time has been kind to him.</i>

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:03.560
<i>I wish I could say the same about myself.</i>

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:06.810
<i>He hasn't changed a bit since then.</i>

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:11.310
<i>That was a few years ago.</i>

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:15.430
<i>This restaurant tucked away in a corner of Rome</i>

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:20.070
<i>unknowingly provided me my second chance to work as a cameriere.</i>

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:57.820
Days of Yore

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:10.690
What's the matter?

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.620
Claudio...

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:17.280
Nicoletta broke Furio's glasses.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:21.440
They fell out of his breast pocket when he bent over, and...

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.660
Snap.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:29.060
I'm so sorry. I didn't look where I was walking...

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:31.000
By the time I realized, it was too late.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.050
Don't apologize. I was careless.

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:38.080
Don't worry about it. They'll be perfectly fine, once I fix them.

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:43.580
Since these were the keepsake that you so kindly gave to me, and all.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:49.350
Thank you for even considering that.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.420
Wait, could those glasses be...

00:04:53.420 --> 00:05:01.500
Yes, Claudio gave them as a gift to Furio when he first started here.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:02.680
What?

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:07.000
I'm sorry, you two... Umm... I...

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:09.480
Don't worry about it.

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:11.870
Now hurry up and pick the herbs.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:15.070
Once you've done that, you've got potatoes to peel.

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:16.680
Right on it, Chef.

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:29.660
Sheesh, she needs to stop behaving like such an amateur.

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:32.460
Everyone's an amateur when they first start.

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:34.960
Try and look at the big picture.

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:39.750
Oh, right. Angela said she wants to stop by tonight.

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:42.100
Think you can keep a table open for her?

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:46.810
Sure. I'm pretty sure we had a cancellation.

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:50.410
If you'd like, I can prepare her usual table.

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:51.790
Grazie.

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:54.120
Is she coming alone? Or...

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.590
It sounds like she's coming with some old friends.

00:05:56.590 --> 00:05:58.610
She said it'll be a party of three.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:04.120
Oh, and my wife requested you as her server.

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:07.020
I don't mind.

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:08.990
Then it's a deal.

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:10.570
Back to work.

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:12.840
All right...

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:20.240
When I am gonna stop making so many mistakes?

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:21.500
Don't beat yourself up.

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:24.650
I'm on dish-washing duty every night.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:27.840
They don't even let me cook food for the staff.

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:33.730
I can teach you how to make a mean cup of espresso.

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:35.390
Thank you.

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:38.850
I bet you never had to worry about this stuff, huh?

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:43.010
No, they were much harsher on me when I was starting out.

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:44.850
I should have expected that answer.

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:53.200
If that's true, then how did you get so used to it?

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.890
That's a fine question.

00:06:57.740 --> 00:06:58.900
You're mean.

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:01.500
That's the spirit.

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:20.130
Buonasera, Angela.

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:22.890
Buonasera, Claudio.

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:25.320
Did you escape the rain?

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:27.570
Come, follow me.

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:33.430
Take good care of us tonight, OK?

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:36.580
I'm glad that you'll be our server.

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:38.290
Th-Thank you.

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:40.430
He's a fan of my husband.

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:43.500
Treat him kindly, would you?

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:50.690
Very well, Madam.

00:07:54.230 --> 00:07:56.530
That was cruel, Furio.

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:58.690
You didn't mention <i>he</i>'d be here.

00:07:59.530 --> 00:08:01.610
Why, whatever do you mean?

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:05.740
OK, this is done. Please take it out there.

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:11.810
I don't see your hands moving!

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:12.910
Get the next plate ready.

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:14.320
Oh, right.

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:19.790
I'm so sorry!

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:21.890
Damn it. Focus on your work!

00:08:26.390 --> 00:08:28.210
<i>Time flies.</i>

00:08:29.170 --> 00:08:32.330
<i>Has it really been over twenty years already?</i>

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:36.690
The Good Old Days

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:41.030
I deeply apologize.

00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:42.160
Claudio!

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:43.490
Back off.

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:46.770
I'm sincerely sorry about that, Madam.

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:50.120
I can't believe he'd do such a thing to Mrs. Rossi,
one of this hotel's best patrons.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:51.400
All is forgiven.

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:04.340
Claudio, Mrs. Rossi, from before, has asked you to come to her room.

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:06.230
She's in room 1201.

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:08.560
But, sir...

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:10.310
Go and get your tongue lashing.

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:16.490
Ma'am, I sincerely apologize for before.

00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:22.870
Stop apologizing.

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:24.580
Relax.

00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:31.910
Since I can't very well have them dock your pay to cover the dress...

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:45.730
Excuse me, Madam...

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:49.430
The restaurant is quite busy at this hour.

00:09:49.430 --> 00:09:51.760
I have to get back to work...

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:54.430
I see. Then we'll have to make this quick.

00:09:54.430 --> 00:09:55.850
I can't.

00:09:55.850 --> 00:09:58.880
Madam, please stop...

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:03.210
A cameriere can't tell me what to do.

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:06.780
You are to pleasure me.

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:08.570
Both tonight and in the future.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:12.310
What do you have to say to that?

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:15.710
Very well, ma'am.

00:10:19.710 --> 00:10:21.820
Don't just stand there, Claudio!

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:23.070
Put these dishes away!

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:24.430
Oh... Yes, sir.

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:29.990
I-I'm sorry.

00:10:29.990 --> 00:10:33.150
You're completely useless, Mr. Santo.

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:35.860
I can smell the woman's perfume on you.

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:38.600
Are you in <i>paradise</i>, Mr. <i>Paradiso?</i>

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:43.500
<i>I'm not feeling well. I haven't eaten since yesterday.</i>

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:48.350
<i>They made me do chores and threw my meal away.</i>

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:11.270
No, no! Don't use lemon, use pepper!

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:21.800
You got a fever or something?

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:27.500
No, I'm just feeling weak since I haven't eaten.

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:38.930
<i>What was that chef's name again?</i>

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:51.240
Hey.

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:56.260
Eat it.

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:05.300
Let me taste it.

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:08.750
Me too.

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:14.400
That's good.

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:17.270
Furio is really something.

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:20.170
He's the head chef here at such a young age.

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:24.860
And I heard he's being flooded with catering requests, too.

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:27.260
Wow...

00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:29.430
<i>He's amazing.</i>

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:35.700
<i>He's younger than I am and yet he's made such a name for himself.</i>

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:37.340
<i>He's well respected, too.</i>

00:12:41.980 --> 00:12:45.660
<i>Maybe I should give up on this cameriere thing.</i>

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:05.830
<i>Should I quit being a cameriere?</i>

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:09.350
<i>Though I've only been at it a few weeks.</i>

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:13.220
I feel bad watching you eat while standing.

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:15.230
Why don't you sit down?

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:18.400
I'll forgive you for it.

00:13:19.160 --> 00:13:21.030
<i>A regular?</i>

00:13:21.710 --> 00:13:24.730
I'm actually not hungry.

00:13:24.730 --> 00:13:28.560
What a waste of such scrumptious-looking food.

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:32.490
You're new, aren't you? I've never seen you before.

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:33.980
What's your name?

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:37.080
Claudio.

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:38.500
Your full name.

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:42.530
Santo Claudio

00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:44.490
Paradiso.

00:13:45.310 --> 00:13:46.760
That's a fine name.

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:49.630
What?

00:13:49.630 --> 00:13:51.190
No, it's just...

00:13:51.190 --> 00:13:54.270
I often get teased for my name.

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:56.360
That blows.

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:59.730
But I'm sure it's not just because of the name.

00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:03.310
You look like you're begging to be picked on.

00:14:03.310 --> 00:14:06.010
Sorry for being so blunt.

00:14:09.060 --> 00:14:13.860
You're right. I desperately want to change my personality.

00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:17.880
I've even begun to think I might not be cut out to be a cameriere...

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:23.120
I realized that while watching Furio, the chef here.

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:25.000
He's so amazing.

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:30.020
I don't think I'll ever get to be like him...

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:34.020
Being a chef and being a cameriere are two different things.

00:14:35.230 --> 00:14:37.630
Right. Of course.

00:14:37.630 --> 00:14:42.770
Why did you decide to become a cameriere? Just for the hell of it?

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:54.800
I think that bringing food to customers, who are so looking forward to dining, is a wonderful thing.

00:14:56.420 --> 00:15:00.470
Furio is Furio. You are you.

00:15:00.470 --> 00:15:04.340
Why not just do what you feel is a wonderful thing?

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:08.050
You have no reason to be bothered so much by it.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:11.380
If it really bothers you, find a new place.

00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:16.460
There are lots of employees here with plenty of connections elsewhere.

00:15:16.460 --> 00:15:18.050
Why not find a new restaurant?

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:21.440
A restaurant that suits you.

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:25.740
My name is Angela,

00:15:25.740 --> 00:15:27.470
Santo Claudio.

00:15:29.170 --> 00:15:30.310
Ciao.

00:15:30.310 --> 00:15:33.240
Would you like me to call Furio out?

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:34.810
Please.

00:15:34.810 --> 00:15:36.830
Who's that girl?

00:15:37.820 --> 00:15:40.260
Oh, that's the daughter of the owner of this hotel.

00:15:40.260 --> 00:15:42.510
She's engaged to Furio.

00:15:47.430 --> 00:15:51.890
<i>It's as if my heart was broken twice in one day.</i>

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:55.800
Here's your dolce.

00:15:57.940 --> 00:15:59.430
Thank you.

00:16:01.930 --> 00:16:03.640
I'm very impressed with Furio.

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:07.470
You can tell he's gotten better with age.

00:16:07.470 --> 00:16:08.970
Right?

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:13.800
And you camerieres are all so refined...

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:17.080
Though, I am curious about why you're all wearing spectacles.

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:21.120
But you can tell Furio chose a great restaurant.

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:23.040
Thank you very much.

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:26.540
Pardon me asking, but where did you do your apprenticeship?

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:31.900
Well... I started off in a hotel ristorante.

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:34.750
You don't say?

00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:39.600
I used to manage a hotel that Angela's father owned.

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:41.690
Fascinating.

00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:46.350
Where'd you go from there?

00:16:46.350 --> 00:16:50.160
Well, I moved from here to there,

00:16:50.160 --> 00:16:53.310
and then spent about twenty years in a small restaurant in the suburbs.

00:16:53.310 --> 00:16:57.520
I actually worked alongside him there, believe it or not.

00:16:59.430 --> 00:17:00.660
You don't say.

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:03.700
It must have been quite the establishment.

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:07.890
But I wish I had you on our staff at the hotel.

00:17:10.570 --> 00:17:13.360
Yes, go and call Furio out here.

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:15.590
I'd definitely like to speak to him tonight.

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:19.400
We can share old battle stories from the hotel.

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:29.430
Weren't you surprised to see him?

00:17:29.430 --> 00:17:32.950
He said he was coming to visit me after all these years,

00:17:32.950 --> 00:17:35.990
so I figured we had to come here.

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:41.000
I know. I almost said something about it when I saw you guys.

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:45.980
Sorry about that. Angela asked me to stay quiet about it.

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:50.820
Even so, your old boss didn't recognize you at all.

00:17:50.820 --> 00:17:54.380
I suppose I should have screwed something up!

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:56.660
You know, break a plate or something.

00:17:57.820 --> 00:17:58.970
You should have!

00:17:58.970 --> 00:18:03.010
Please. You didn't remember him when you saw him, either.

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:10.110
Oh, yeah... So many people came through that hotel's doors, so...

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:14.040
No, I was only there a short time.

00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:18.180
I was amazed you remembered me at all.

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:21.130
I never forget a face,

00:18:21.130 --> 00:18:24.250
even if we only meet for a moment.

00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:27.640
Besides, we talked to each other back then, remember?

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:29.380
I remember it well.

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:33.170
Also, your mood hadn't changed a bit then.

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:38.590
I was always so worn and haggered,

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:40.400
until I came here.

00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:44.850
I thought I told you not to worry about those things.

00:18:46.460 --> 00:18:49.680
Did you find a good restaurant to work at?

00:18:52.620 --> 00:18:53.810
I did.

00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:04.790
That was fantastic.

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:12.740
Oh, Claudio.

00:19:13.950 --> 00:19:16.270
Wh-What's wrong?

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:24.200
Actually, Teo said that since we're going to be thinking up a spring menu,

00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:27.360
I should think of a dish to serve the staff!

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:33.570
Congratulations. That's fantastic news.

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:38.460
She can't stay an amateur forever.

00:19:39.180 --> 00:19:42.840
I'll try to not be too critical of you, though.

00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:47.080
I feel rejuvenated somehow!

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:49.960
Like I have to get to work on this right away!

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:51.720
Good luck.

00:19:51.720 --> 00:19:54.330
Thanks. Look forward to it.

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:58.530
Oh, if it's all right, could you taste it before I show it to him?

00:19:58.530 --> 00:20:01.000
Sure. I'd be happy to.

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:04.920
See you tomorrow, then. Ciao!

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:33.020
<i>I lost some things along the way, but I met many new faces, as well.</i>

00:20:33.020 --> 00:20:37.640
<i>Somehow the sands of time have brought me here, to dell'orso.</i>

00:20:46.040 --> 00:20:48.240
<i>Now, to me anyway,</i>

00:20:48.240 --> 00:20:52.660
<i>this restaurant is the happy place that calms my soul.</i>

00:20:56.880 --> 00:21:15.560
Day Off from the Ristorante

00:21:05.890 --> 00:21:08.050
The presentation is nice...

00:21:08.050 --> 00:21:09.530
...but it tastes like crap.

00:21:10.680 --> 00:21:14.070
M-M-Maybe I overcooked the eggs...

00:21:14.070 --> 00:21:15.580
You lack fundamentals.

00:22:44.570 --> 00:22:47.580
M-M-Maybe you'll watch next time...
